    description: "The taint walk treats builtins.print as terminating (keeps nothing, writes nowhere) even when it has file=. `print(secret, file=fh)` writes to the file object, so a flow through it is a sink, and a walk refuting through it is wrong.\n\nSeen by the WI-bamuj build agent (evidence fast_smart_test_build_11172026/bamuj/). Not measured on a fixture with a claim yet.\n\nCLOSE WHEN a fixture `print(os.getenv(\"K\"), file=open(p, \"w\"))` reads violated against host_secret -> host_fs, with a no-file= control, and the summary row for print states the file= case."  # e02b
